      "content": "Your frustration stems from a desperate need to see action in the face of uncertainty, which makes any feeling of hope feel hollow and disconnected from the reality you see. However, focusing on immediate safety and keeping your mind sharp often prepares you to help, eventually, stabilize your specific community or protect those around you in tangible ways. Even if the full scale of the disaster feels hopeless, many people find strength in refusing to let daily suffering overshadow the fragile moments of grace available right now.",
